From: Orkhan Javadli <ojavadli@gmail.com>
Date: Sat, 8 Aug 2026 13:01:56 -0700
Subject: [PATCH 39/50] tei-v7 prompt-19: Reproduction-first execution gate
 with explicit fallback

---
 Orcar/prompts.py | 2 +-
 1 file changed, 1 insertion(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/Orcar/prompts.py b/Orcar/prompts.py
index 51909c5..e8f12a2 100644
--- a/Orcar/prompts.py
+++ b/Orcar/prompts.py
@@ -1,6 +1,6 @@
 STEP_EXAMPLE = {
     "execution_gate": {
-        "before_patch": "Do not localize or edit until you have executed and recorded a minimal reproducer when the repository permits it. Preserve the exact command, exit status, exception type, actual output, expected output, repository revision, and configuration. Treat unexecuted issue claims as hypotheses, not facts. Then separate confirmed observations from hypotheses; preserve the exact reproducer, expected and actual behavior, exception type, first project-owned stack frame, and relevant version or configuration; then rank candidate symbols by which one directly transforms the triggering input into the violated output: record the exact failing command, exit status, exception, relevant output, repository revision, and independently confirmed minimal reproducer; extract the issue's explicit behavioral predicates and constraints; identify the first project-owned frame and the nearest caller/callee; list relevant definitions, tests, and configuration or version gates; separate confirmed facts from hypotheses; and state which missing artifact would most strongly discriminate competing targets.",
+        "before_patch": "Before proposing a location or edit, execute the smallest available reproducer and record the exact command, exit status, exception, relevant output, revision, and configuration. If reproduction is impossible, explicitly record why, switch to a static-evidence plan, and require a focused regression test or equivalent executable check before accepting any patch. Preserve the exact command, exit status, exception type, actual output, expected output, repository revision, and configuration. Treat unexecuted issue claims as hypotheses, not facts. Then separate confirmed observations from hypotheses; preserve the exact reproducer, expected and actual behavior, exception type, first project-owned stack frame, and relevant version or configuration; then rank candidate symbols by which one directly transforms the triggering input into the violated output: record the exact failing command, exit status, exception, relevant output, repository revision, and independently confirmed minimal reproducer; extract the issue's explicit behavioral predicates and constraints; identify the first project-owned frame and the nearest caller/callee; list relevant definitions, tests, and configuration or version gates; separate confirmed facts from hypotheses; and state which missing artifact would most strongly discriminate competing targets.",
         "after_patch": "After editing, run the smallest regression oracle that directly reproduces the reported behavior and record the exact command, exit status, and relevant output. A patch is not complete unless the original failure is resolved and the expected result is observed. If the oracle fails, inspect the diff, compare the actual result with the predicted result, and revise or revert the patch rather than declaring success; then run one nearby valid-input check, one boundary or nested-input check, and one structurally different case that exercises the same semantic path, such as a nested expression, unevaluated form, symbolic parameter, or alternate container type. For each check, state the expected result before execution and investigate any deviation before finalizing. the focused repository test before finalizing",
         "compatibility_checks": ["nearby valid input", "boundary or nested input", "focused repository test", "alternate representation or assumption", "interaction with the nearest caller", "symbolic versus numeric or concrete evaluation", "unevaluated versus automatically evaluated form", "commutative versus noncommutative symbols when relevant", "assumptions, domains, and type-dependent behavior", "repeated application or simplification/idempotence", "order, shape, and dimensionality preservation", "serialization or pretty-printing if representation is part of the issue"],
         "acceptance_rule": "A patch is resolved only when: (1) the pre-patch failure is reproduced with a recorded command, input, exception or output, and exit status; (2) the patch is applied to the intended symbol and the diff is inspected; (3) the exact original command is rerun and now produces the stated expected output or exception; (4) a focused regression test passes; (5) at least one nearby valid case and one boundary or nested case pass; and (6) the final diff contains no unrelated changes. If any item is missing or fails, report unresolved, preserve the failing evidence, and do not claim success.",
